Good catch, and no — it doesn't. `App.clipboard` (in `[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]`) is a plain in-memory JS array, not `navigator.clipboard` (the real OS/system clipboard). It only exists inside one page's JS state, so it's scoped to a single tab/window — copying in one Tonncade window and pasting in a separate window (or tab) can't work, since they don't share any memory. It was only ever built for moving cells *between modes within one running session*, never advertised as cross-window.

Want me to wire it to the real OS clipboard (`navigator.clipboard.writeText`/`readText`, e.g. as JSON) so copy/paste works across separate windows/tabs too? That's a distinct, real feature, not a bug fix. I'll finish the test-timeout issue I just hit first, then come back to this if you want it.
